    "text": "In YDSE arrangement as shown in the figure, fringes are seen on screen using monochromatic source S having wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></math> (in the air). <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are two slits separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>mm</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . Left of slits <math><msub><mrow><mtext>S</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mtext>a</mtext><mtext>n</mtext><mtext>d</mtext><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>S</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> medium of refractive index <math><msub><mrow><mtext>n</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is present and to the right of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> medium of <math><msub><mrow><mtext>n</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , is present. A thin slab of thickness 't' is placed in front of <math><msub><mrow><mtext>S</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The refractive index of <math><msub><mrow><mtext>n</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> of the slab varies with distance from it's starting face as shown in figure.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image9-7fc148ea-3403-4733-920d-9660674a9c9a.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 164px;\" /><br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image10-f7b86f21-103e-4d63-af43-664ffe75c296.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 124px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rIn order to get central maxima at the centre of the screen, the thickness of the slab (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>) required is:<br />\r&nbsp;",
